Subject: [PATCH 24/38] fs: sharedfs: writes

Create, mkdir, symlink, unlink, rmdir, rename and setattr go to the host
as requests; the host performs them on the directory and updates the
index before answering, so the guest instantiates the new entry from
the index and refreshes the affected inodes from it. A shrinking
truncate breaks the DAX layout of the range being dropped before the
host truncates, as truncation does on any DAX file system.

Each inode type gets its own operations table, as C file systems do: a
regular file must not carry `get_link`, since the dcache takes any
non-directory inode with one for a symbolic link. Writes stamp the
inode's times through `file_update_time`.

